    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized tutoring, explain concepts in simple language, and generate practice problems tailored to a student’s level. They can help students explore different problem-solving paths and reduce anxiety by providing immediate feedback. However, they should complement—not replace—human teachers who can guide deeper understanding and critical thinking."
